erent  from what they are within the earth they  undergo phase transitions that do not  happen within the earth  that has a dramatic effect on  the planetary interior structure and on  the planet  properties  what it tells us is that the fact that  we see a super earth  behind our solar system and that  super earth is in the hobby double zone  which is defined as the distance from  the  from the star that allows for water to  be liquid  it doesn't necessarily mean that that  planet is habitable  just because you know if it is too big  or too small  that interior structure may be  completely different  so that generate a planet that is very  different  from the earth  [Music]

